==International channels==
{{see also|Disney XD (international)}}
Disney XD, similarly born of a merger between [[Jetix]] and [[Toon Disney]],<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.broadbandtvnews.com/2009/02/16/french-jetix-becomes-disney-xd/ |title=French Jetix becomes Disney XD |work=Broadband TV News |date=February 16, 2009 |access-date=27 August 2018 |first=Robert |last=Briel |archive-date=January 22, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250122183458/https://www.broadbandtvnews.com/2009/02/16/french-jetix-becomes-disney-xd/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Chmielewski |first=Dawn C. |url=https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-2008-aug-07-fi-disney7-story.html |title=Enough with the girls, tween boys get their own brand of Disney love |access-date=February 25, 2014 |newspaper=[[Los Angeles Times]] |date=August 7, 2008 |archive-date=September 30, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200930193135/https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-2008-aug-07-fi-disney7-story.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite journal |title=Benjamin's buttons. Disneys global boss hit the right keys |url=https://www.thefreelibrary.com/Benjamin%27s+buttons.+Disneys+global+boss+hit+the+right+keys.-a0210520144 |access-date=April 9, 2014 |journal=[[VideoAge International]] |date=October 1, 2009 |publisher=TV Trade Media, Inc. |via=[[The Free Library]] |archive-date=August 9, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160809172052/http://www.thefreelibrary.com/Benjamin%27s+buttons.+Disneys+global+boss+hit+the+right+keys.-a0210520144 |url-status=live }}</ref> was formerly available around the world. Most of the international Disney XD networks have been closed since 2019, due to the launch of [[Disney+]].

On January 6, 2019, Disney XD closed in Australia and New Zealand with programs moving to [[Disney Channel (Australia & New Zealand)|Disney Channel]] for that network's last year before shutting down itself with its content being subsumed into Disney+. In India, the channel was rebranded as [[Marvel HQ]] on January 9, 2019 which was later rebranded as [[Super Hungama]] on March 1, 2022. On October 1, 2019, Disney XD closed in Italy following the non-renewal of its [[Sky Italia|Sky]] carriage agreement.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.dday.it/redazione/32502/sky-tv-famiglia-canali-fox-disney-xd|title=Basta Disney XD e Fox Comedy su Sky: dal 1 ottobre spenti cinque canali Fox e Disney|website=DDay.it|access-date=September 30, 2019|archive-date=September 30, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190930013341/https://www.dday.it/redazione/32502/sky-tv-famiglia-canali-fox-disney-xd|url-status=live}}</ref>

The Spanish and German versions were closed on April 1, 2020, followed by France's network a week later. XD in Singapore closed on June 1, 2020,<ref>{{Cite web|orig-date=June 2, 2020|title=Disney channels go dark in Singapore|url=https://www.contentasia.tv/news/disney-channels-go-dark-singapore|access-date=February 12, 2022|website=ContentAsia|language=en|archive-date=February 12, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220212051340/https://www.contentasia.tv/news/disney-channels-go-dark-singapore|url-status=live}}</ref> then the British and continental Africa domestic feeds on October 1, 2020.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2020/06/disney-to-close-kids-channels-in-the-uk-following-launch-of-disney-1202969592/|title=Disney To Close Kids Channels In The UK Following Launch Of Disney+|first=Jake|last=Kanter|date=June 25, 2020|access-date=September 26, 2020|archive-date=November 16, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231116233841/https://deadline.com/2020/06/disney-to-close-kids-channels-in-the-uk-following-launch-of-disney-1202969592/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://teeveetee.blogspot.com/2020/09/going-dark-on-dstv-disneys-fox-life-and.html|title=TV with Thinus: Going dark on DStv: Disney's FOX Life and Disney XD the next TV channels leaving MultiChoice's pay-TV service at the end of September 2020.|date=September 7, 2020|access-date=January 1, 2021|archive-date=July 9, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210709182452/https://teeveetee.blogspot.com/2020/09/going-dark-on-dstv-disneys-fox-life-and.html|url-status=live}}</ref> The [[Disney XD (Southeast Asia)|Southeast Asian]], [[Disney XD (Scandinavia)|Scandinavian]], and Middle Eastern feeds closed on December 31, 2020. The Japanese and Turkish channels also closed on January 31, 2021.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://whatsondisneyplus.com/disney-xd-to-close-down-in-japan/|title=Disney XD To Close Down In Japan &#124; What's On Disney Plus|date=October 21, 2020|access-date=January 26, 2021|archive-date=May 16, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210516052103/https://whatsondisneyplus.com/disney-xd-to-close-down-in-japan/|url-status=live}}</ref> The [[Disney XD (Latin America)|Latin American]] feed closed on March 31, 2022. The [[Disney XD (Netherlands)|Netherlands]] feed closed on May 1, 2025.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kriek |first=Jarco |date=2025-04-17 |title=Canal Digitaal voert zenderwijziging door en haalt 192TV uit aanbod, Museum TV 4K nieuw |url=https://www.totaaltv.nl/nieuws/canal-digitaal-voert-zenderwijziging-door-en-haalt-192tv-uit-aanbod-museum-tv-4k-nieuw/ |access-date=2025-04-17 |website=Totaal TV |language=nl}}</ref> 

The latest closure was in [[Disney XD (Canada)|Canada]] on September 1, 2025. Since then, Disney XD only has one international channel operating in [[Disney XD (Poland)|Poland]].

